<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Eldredgeops rana_17file Turing wavelength at 342 nm (Tioughniogan, 384 Ma) (Eldredgeops rana_17file)",
        "Eldredgeops rana_17file Turing wavelength at 342 nm (Tioughniogan, 384 Ma) faithfully reproduces Eldredgeops rana_17file morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eldredgeops rana_17file specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eldredgeops rana_17file" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 342 nm was measured on an Eldredgeops lens, or that the gallery JPEG is a 342 nm micrograph.",
        "does_not_claim: That the pass-1 raw activator profile is a fitted specimen match.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Physical wavelength 342 nm is the length-unit definition at this parameter point, not a measurement from a Devonian thin section.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters rho_a=0.082, rho_b=0.918, D_u=0.060, D_v=1.200 and a periodic cell of side 1.15 lambda_c.",
        "reported_in_source: Eldredge 1972 documents a step from 18 to 17 dorsoventral lens files between the Cazenovian and Tioughniogan horizons.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber when the two morphogens diffuse at different rates.",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery plate is a radial ocellus luminance field with a labeled 100 micrometre bar. Radial shape is compared in dimensionless radius." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Eldredgeops rana_17file (Middle Devonian (Tioughniogan, 384 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Eldredgeops" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/eldredgeops_rana_17file_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Eldredgeops rana_17file; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber when the two morphogens diffuse at different rates. | Eldredge 1972 documents a step from 18 to 17 dorsoventral lens files between the Cazenovian and Tioughniogan horizons.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters rho_a=0.082, rho_b=0.918, D_u=0.060, D_v=1.200 and a periodic cell of side 1.15 lambda_c. | Physical wavelength 342 nm is the length-unit definition at this parameter point, not a measurement from a Devonian thin section.; transfer_boundary: The gallery plate is a radial ocellus luminance field with a labeled 100 micrometre bar. Radial shape is compared in dimensionless radius.; does_not_claim: That 342 nm was measured on an Eldredgeops lens, or that the gallery JPEG is a 342 nm micrograph. | That the pass-1 raw activator profile is a fitted specimen match.]; other sources: Systematics and evolution of Phacops rana (Green, 1832) and Phacops iowensis Delo, 1935, from the Middle Devonian of North America <https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/1096>; phenomenon_size: 357 nm (3.57e-07 m, log10=-6.447 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 357 nm to 803 µm): 357 nm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-bioelectric-polarity, 1.1 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-vertex-packing, 18 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength, 36 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-clock-wavefront, 80 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-morphogen-condensation, 98 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-elastic-buckling, 112 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-flux-canalization, 156 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1473-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5531/sd.paleo.7> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://paleobiodb.org/classic/checkTaxonInfo?taxon_name=Eldredgeops>,
        <https://www.morphosource.org/Search/index?search=Eldredgeops> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Trilobite Segmentation & Eye Fossil Series" ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 3.84e+02 ;
